      "text": "To determine the month in which Hal will change the batteries on the 25th time, we need to calculate the pattern of when the batteries are replaced and specifically identify the 25th occurrence.\n\n1. **Identify the periodicity \\( T \\) and the position \\( k \\):**\n   - Hal changes the batteries every 5 months.\n   - We need to find the month for the 25th replacement.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of months \\( T_k \\) after \\( k \\) changes:**\n   - Each battery change happens after an interval of 5 months.\n   - Therefore, for \\( k \\) changes, the total number of months is:\n     \\[\n     T_k = 5 \\times k\n     \\]\n   - For \\( k = 25 \\) changes:\n     \\[\n     T_{25} = 5 \\times 25 = 125 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Convert the total months into a calendar year:**\n   - We need to convert 125 months into a specific month. \n   - There are 12 months in a year.\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of years:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of years} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{125}{12} \\right\\rfloor = 10 \\text{ years}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine the month within the 10 years:**\n   - Start with May and add 125 months.\n   - We need to calculate the day of the month within those 125 months from May.\n\n6. **Check for a leap year:**\n   - A leap year occurs every 4 years. Within 10 years, there are:\n     \\[\n     \\left\\lfloor \\frac{10}{4} \\right\\rfloor = 2 \\text{ leap years}\n     \\]\n   - Each leap year adds 30 days to the calendar.\n\n7. **Calculate the day of the year within the 125 months:**\n   - Start from May 1st.\n   - 125 months means 10 years and a quarter of the year.\n   - Each quarter is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{125}{4} = 31 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n8. **Daily counting for the 10 years:**\n   - Since there are 365 days in a year:\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 365 = 3650 \\text{ days}\n     \\]\n   - After 10 years:\n     \\[\n     3650 \\text{ days in 10 years} = 3650 \\mod 366 = 359 \\text{ days left}\n     \\]\n   - Continue counting the days:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Days of the month} = 1 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 31 + 359 = 359 \\text{ days}\n     \\]\n     - Day of May: \\( 359 - 365 = -6 \\)\n     - Adjusting for the new year:\n     - Days in June: \\( 6 + 31 = 37 \\)\n     - Days in the first part of July: \\( 37 + 31 = 68 \\)\n     - Days in the second part of July: \\( 68 + 25 = 93 \\)\n     - Days in August: \\( 93 \\)\n\n9. **Convert to weeks and days:**\n   - \\( 93 \\div 7 = 13 \\text{ weeks and } 2 \\text{ days} \\)\n\nThus, the batteries will be changed on the 93rd day of the month in August, which falls on \\(\\boxed{06}\\), meaning the April day in August:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{June}\n\\]",
