      "text": "The batteries are changed every 5 months, so for 25 changes, they will be changed in the 25 * 5 = 125th month. If the first change was in May, then the 25th change will be in the 125th month - 5 month increments until we find a match. \n\nLet's calculate how many 5-month increments are needed to reach the 125th month:\n125 months / 5 months per change = 25 changes\n\nSince the first change was in May, adding 20 increments of 5 months will get us to a multiple of 12 (as 5 * 20 = 100, and 125 - 100 = 25):\nMay (1st change)\nJul (5th month increment)\nOct (10th month increment)\nJan (15th month increment)\nApr (20th month increment, which is a multiple of 12)\nMoving past this point, we see that there is no further increment of 20 months. Therefore, the 25th change will occur in the next month after Apr, which is May.\n\nThus, the batteries will be changed the 25th time in \\boxed{May}.",
