      "text": "To determine the month when Hal will need to change the batteries the 25th time, we start by noting that he changes them every 5 months and he changed them in May (the 1st time). We need to find the 25th such event.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of 5-month periods in 25 years:\n\\[\n\\frac{25}{5} = 5\n\\]\nThis means that the batteries will be changed every 5 months for a total of 25 times. To find the month, we need to determine the cumulative number of months added over these 5 periods.\n\nEach period is 5 months long:\n\\[\n5 \\times 5 = 25 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\nHal changed the batteries in May, so we add 25 months to May to find the month of the 25th change:\n\\[\n2023 - \\text{May}\\text{ + 25 months}\n\\]\n\nWe map 25 months to the month system:\n\\[\n25 \\text{ months} = 3 \\text{ years and 1 month}\n\\]\n\nStarting from May:\n- 1 year ago in May: April\n- 2 years ago in May: March\n- 3 years ago in May: February\n\nTherefore, adding 3 years and 1 month to May:\n\\[\n\\text{May} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{June}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{June} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{July}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{July} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{August}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{August} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{September}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{September} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{October}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{October} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{November}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{November} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{December}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{December} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{January}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{January} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{February}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{February} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{March}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{March} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{April}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{April} + 1 \\text{ year} \\rightarrow \\text{May}\n\\]\n\nThus, after adding 25 months from the initial May change, the batteries will be changed again during:\n\\boxed{\\text{May}}",
