      "text": "Hal replaces the batteries every 5 months. He changed them for the first time in May. To determine the month when the batteries will be changed for the 25th time, we need to calculate the total number of months that have passed.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of months for the 25th change:\n\\[\n25 \\text{ changes} \\times 5 \\text{ months per change} = 125 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the month that is 125 months after May. We will break down the 125 months into larger units (years and months) and calculate the remainder to find out the exact month.\n\n1. Calculate the number of complete years in 125 months:\n\\[\n125 \\div 12 = 10 \\text{ years and } 5 \\text{ months}\n\\]\nThis means 10 full years will pass, and 5 months will remain.\n\n2. Determine the month in 10 years following May:\nSince 125 months include 10 years, we will count the months one by one until we reach the 5th month.\n\\[\n\\text{May, June, July, August, September, October, November, December, January, February, March, April, May}\n\\]\nWe see that after May, the next month is June. Therefore, 125 months after May will be in the month of June.\n\nThus, the batteries will be changed for the 25th time in the month of \\boxed{June}.",
